WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.360
How does a cluster of machines agree on one shared truth, even when a node crashes or the network splits them apart?

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:14.774
This is Raft, the consensus algorithm behind gimle mimir, Gimle's replicated state store.

00:00:15.674 --> 00:00:18.338
Every node starts out as a follower.

00:00:18.338 --> 00:00:24.408
Each one runs its own randomized election timer, between 150 and 300 milliseconds.

00:00:24.408 --> 00:00:35.066
If node A doesn't hear from a leader before its timer fires, it assumes there isn't one, becomes a candidate, and asks its peers to vote for it.

00:00:35.966 --> 00:00:39.064
Node B and Node C don't just vote blindly.

00:00:39.064 --> 00:00:44.303
Each one checks that Node A's log is at least as up to date as its own.

00:00:44.303 --> 00:00:46.737
Only then does it grant its vote.

00:00:46.737 --> 00:00:52.197
This is what stops a node with stale data from ever taking over as leader.

00:00:53.097 --> 00:00:57.713
Two votes out of three is a majority, so Node A becomes the leader.

00:00:57.713 --> 00:01:05.360
From now on, it sends a heartbeat to every follower every 50 milliseconds, asserting that it's still in charge.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:12.593
A follower stuck in a network partition, unable to reach a majority, can never elect itself leader alone.

00:01:13.493 --> 00:01:18.411
Now a client proposes a write, say, registering a new deployment.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.756
Only the leader accepts writes.

00:01:20.756 --> 00:01:23.934
It appends the entry to its own log first.

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:33.178
Next, the leader replicates that log entry out to every follower, over the same append entries message its heartbeats already use.

00:01:34.078 --> 00:01:41.929
Once a majority of nodes, not all of them, just a majority, have acknowledged the entry, it's considered committed.

00:01:41.929 --> 00:01:47.459
It's applied to the state machine, and only then is the client finally unblocked.

00:01:47.459 --> 00:01:54.422
A minority can never commit anything alone, and that single rule is what makes split brain impossible.

00:01:55.322 --> 00:02:02.266
That's leader election and log replication in Raft, and exactly how gimle mimir implements both.

00:02:02.266 --> 00:02:12.753
The full concepts page goes further: snapshotting, live membership changes, and a real split brain bug this project's own tests caught and fixed.

00:02:12.753 --> 00:02:13.983
Link in the docs.

